// bike.fm: the vehicle as a motorcycle (car.kind Motorcycle, car.model 1): everything from the crank to the road, in
// a straight line, on two wheels.
//
// The bodies: the crank (the engine's; its speed comes in and goes out of step()); the gearbox's output, at the rear
// wheel's side of the chain, with the clutch's basket, the gears and the sprockets' inertia on it; the rear wheel,
// driven; the front wheel, free; the bike with its rider. Between them:
//
//   the clutch: a wet multi-plate clutch (a coupling, diff.fm's law) from the crank through the overall ratio (the
//   primary drive, the gear, the sprockets) to the output, at the gears' and the chain's efficiency whichever way the
//   power goes. Its capacity is `clutchTorque` (0: 1.35 times the engine's peak) times the rider's lever, times the
//   launch helper (it closes with the revs from just over idle, as the vehicle model's robotised clutch: a rider who
//   never stalls). Once it has locked in a gear it is held closed by the gearbox output's speed through the gear (not
//   the crank's), until a shift, neutral, the lever pulled or that speed at the stall band's foot: so it does not slip
//   again when the revs sag lugging a tall gear or on the overrun. The output's speed, not the road's: a rear tyre that
//   locks takes the output down with it, and the latch lets go before the engine stalls, as a rider would. Open, its oil still drags: 0.6 % of its capacity (judgement: a wet clutch creeps a little cold); a dry one
//   (`clutchDry`) does not.
//   A slipper clutch passes backwards (the wheel driving the engine) only `slipperTorque` of its capacity: its ramps
//   lift the pressure plate when the back torque is more, so a downshift that would spin the engine up hard slips the
//   clutch instead of the tyre. Without one the clutch passes its whole capacity both ways.
//   the chain (chain.fm): a spring with play from the output to the rear wheel; the play closing is an event.
//   the brakes: the lever (ctl.brake) on the front, `brakeDecel` at a full pull; the pedal (ctl.handbrake) on the rear,
//   (1 - `brakeBias`) of that; ABS as the vehicle model's. The rolling resistance holds each wheel as a brake does.
//   the tyres (tyre.fm): each pushes the bike by its tread's deflection. `bikeTyre` sets their grip (the peak
//   longitudinal friction on dry asphalt, warm, at the compound's nominal load: touring 1.10, sport 1.25, hypersport
//   1.40, race slick 1.55, dual sport 1.00, cruiser 1.05: judgement, in the range Cossalter's Motorcycle Dynamics, 2nd
//   ed., ch. 2, gives for motorcycle tyres on dry asphalt, ordered by compound) and the curve's shape (the vehicle's motorcycle compound; a slick's for race slicks).
//
// The pitch. The bike and rider are one body; their centre of mass is `b` ahead of the rear tyre's contact and `h` up
// (the bike's and the rider's, by their masses; a tuck lowers the rider and moves them forward). With both wheels down
// the load moves rearward by m a h / L (lagged 30 ms: a sport bike's chain pull holds the rear up, so the load arrives nearly at once) and forward under braking; the front's load
// cannot fall below zero, nor the rear's (a stoppie: flagged, not modelled further). When the rear tyre pushes the bike
// harder than g b / h, the front lifts: the bike turns about the rear contact,
//
//     (I + m (x^2 + y^2)) theta'' = m a y - m g x,      x = b cos(theta) - h sin(theta),  y = b sin(theta) + h cos(theta)
//
// (theta nose up, a the bike's acceleration, I `pitchInertia` about the centre of mass) until it comes down (the landing
// takes its rate) or passes the balance point (x = 0: it loops; held at 80 degrees and flagged). A lifted bike still
// accelerates at what its rear tyre gives: the front's lift takes none of it. So the launch is the wheelie's: a rider or
// an anti-wheelie control holds the front at `wheelieAngle` by easing the throttle (a lagged loop on the pitch and its
// rate, through the pedal the engine is given; it eases it too when the rear spins, as a rider or a traction control
// does) or by slipping the clutch (its capacity held to what keeps the pitch's acceleration at a damped return to the
// angle, and to the rear tyre's grip: a launch that dumps the lever is then a good one). A slipping clutch passes its
// capacity, not the engine's torque, so only the clutch's way holds a launch while the lever is still coming out.
//
// The gearbox: sequential, `gears` ratios (`ratio[]`, or with `autoGearing` a sport bike's six: 2.62, 2.00, 1.68,
// 1.45, 1.30, 1.18), worked by the shift counters, a press at a time (one made during a shift waits for it): up
// from neutral is first, down from first neutral. An upshift with
// the throttle open and the quickshifter on is clutchless: the ignition is cut for `quickshiftCut` (through the ECU's
// cut), the dogs come out as the load comes off, the next gear's go in at 40 % of the cut, the clutch stays in.
// Without it (or with the throttle shut) the rider pulls the clutch (open by 35 ms), shuts the throttle for 60 ms, the
// gear goes in at 50 ms and the clutch comes back by 160 ms. A downshift with the auto-blipper is clutchless too: the
// throttle is blipped to the lower gear's speed (through the pedal the engine is given) for 100 ms, the dogs in at
// 60 ms. Without it the rider pulls the clutch as above and lets it out over 100 ms with no blip: a clumsy downshift,
// whose back torque spins the engine up through the clutch, and with no slipper can lock or hop the rear tyre (the
// load has moved forward, off it). A downshift that would take the engine past 97 % of its redline is refused.
//
// Not modelled: steering, lean, the suspension's own travel (only its lag), the rear's squat from the chain's pull,
// a wheelie's gyroscopic effects, the rider falling off.
//
//   b.setup(rate); b.apply(); b.configure(jE, peakTq, idleW, redW); b.control(...) every 16;
//   w = b.step(w, tq, dt, jCrank) (the crank's inertia now, 0 for configure's);
//   y = b.road(); for the engine: b.pedalOut(gas, wCrankAvg), b.cutWanted(), b.blipSpeed(), b.lashStrike()
#pragma once
#include "vehicle.fm"
#include "bspec.fm"
#include "chain.fm"

// a sport bike's six gearbox ratios (before the primary and the chain)
const float BIKE_RATIOS[6] = {2.62f, 2.00f, 1.68f, 1.45f, 1.30f, 1.18f};
// each tyre choice: its grip on dry asphalt, and the compound whose curve and heat it borrows
const float BIKE_TYRE_MU[BIKE_TYRES] = {1.10f, 1.25f, 1.40f, 1.55f, 1.00f, 1.05f};
const int BIKE_TYRE_COMPOUND[BIKE_TYRES] = {9, 9, 9, 4, 9, 9};

// The gearbox's logic, every 16 samples
module BikeBox
{
    int n;
    float r[VEH_GEARS];
    float primary;
    float chain;        // rear teeth over front
    int gear;           // 0 N, 1 to n
    bool shifting;
    int to;
    bool up;
    bool byClutch;      // this shift is the rider's, with the clutch
    float t;
    float tIn;          // when the dogs went in
    float robot;        // the clutch as the shift and the launch helper leave it, 0 open to 1
    bool synced;        // the launch helper's clutch has synchronised in this gear: held closed by the output's speed
                        // until a shift, neutral, the lever or a stall (card D's patch for B2, the lead's ruling, 25 Nov)
    float rollOff;      // the rider's throttle through a clutch upshift, 0 shut to 1
    bool cut;
    float cutTime;
    float blip;         // the crank speed asked for, rad/s (0: none)
    int lastUp;
    int lastDown;
    bool seen;
    int upshifts;
    int quickshifts;
    int blips;

    void reset()
    {
        gear = 0;
        shifting = false;
        to = 0;
        t = 0.0f;
        robot = 1.0f;
        synced = false;
        rollOff = 1.0f;
        cut = false;
        blip = 0.0f;
        seen = false;
    }

    float ratioOf(int g)
    {
        if (g <= 0)
            return 0.0f;
        const int k = g > n ? n : g;
        return primary * r[k - 1] * chain;
    }

    void control(float d16, int upCount, int downCount, float pedal, float w, float wOut, float idleW, float redW,
                 bool quick, bool autoBlip, float engage)
    {
        if (!seen)
        {
            seen = true;
            lastUp = upCount;
            lastDown = downCount;
        }
        // the presses, one at a time: one made during a shift waits for it to end
        int ups = 0;
        int downs = 0;
        if (upCount < lastUp)
            lastUp = upCount;
        if (downCount < lastDown)
            lastDown = downCount;
        if (!shifting)
        {
            if (upCount > lastUp)
            {
                ups = 1;
                lastUp += 1;
            }
            else if (downCount > lastDown)
            {
                downs = 1;
                lastDown += 1;
            }
        }
        // the launch helper: closes with the revs from just over idle (the vehicle model's)
        const float x = fminf(fmaxf((w - idleW - 15.7f) / 94.2f, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        float launch = x * x * (3.0f - 2.0f * x);
        // (once synchronised it is no launch, as the vehicle model's paddles (gearbox.fm, `synced`): once the clutch has
        // locked in this gear (the slip under 0.5 rad/s, engaged) it is held closed by the output's speed through the gear,
        // opening only as that nears the idle (50 to 250 rpm over it), until a shift begins, neutral, the lever pulled
        // (engage under 0.5) or the output's speed at the stall band's foot. Here the output's speed carries the rear
        // tyre's slip (the vehicle model's reads the road's); B2 may pass the road's instead)
        const float gIn = ratioOf(gear);
        const float wGear = fabsf(gIn * wOut);
        if (gear == 0 || shifting || engage < 0.5f || wGear < idleW + 5.2f)
            synced = false;
        else if (fabsf(w - wGear) < 0.5f && robot > 0.1f)
            synced = true;
        if (synced)
        {
            const float xr = fminf(fmaxf((wGear - idleW - 5.2f) / 20.9f, 0.0f), 1.0f);
            launch = fmaxf(launch, xr * xr * (3.0f - 2.0f * xr));
        }
        if (!shifting)
        {
            if (ups > 0)
            {
                if (gear == 0)
                    gear = 1;
                else if (gear < n)
                {
                    shifting = true;
                    up = true;
                    to = gear + 1;
                    t = 0.0f;
                    byClutch = !(quick && pedal > 0.1f);
                    upshifts += 1;
                    if (!byClutch)
                        quickshifts += 1;
                }
            }
            else if (downs > 0)
            {
                if (gear == 1)
                    gear = 0;
                else if (gear > 1 && fabsf(wOut * ratioOf(gear - 1)) < 0.97f * redW)
                {
                    shifting = true;
                    up = false;
                    to = gear - 1;
                    t = 0.0f;
                    byClutch = !autoBlip;
                    if (!byClutch)
                        blips += 1;
                }
            }
        }
        robot = gear != 0 ? launch : 1.0f;
        rollOff = 1.0f;
        cut = false;
        blip = 0.0f;
        if (!shifting)
            return;
        t += d16;
        if (byClutch)
        {
            // the rider: the clutch open by 35 ms, the gear in at 50 ms, the clutch out from 60 ms (by 160 ms)
            if (t >= 0.05f)
                gear = to;
            const float open = t < 0.035f ? 1.0f - t / 0.035f : (t < 0.06f ? 0.0f : fminf((t - 0.06f) / 0.1f, 1.0f));
            robot = launch * open;
            if (up && t < 0.06f)
                rollOff = 0.0f;
            if (t >= 0.16f)
                shifting = false;
            return;
        }
        robot = 1.0f;
        if (up)
        {
            // the quickshifter: the cut, the dogs out at once and the next in at 40 % of it
            gear = t >= 0.4f * cutTime ? to : 0;
            cut = t < cutTime;
            if (t >= cutTime)
            {
                shifting = false;
                cut = false;
            }
        }
        else
        {
            // the auto-blipper: the throttle to the lower gear's speed; the dogs in once the engine is there (15 ms at the
            // soonest, 100 ms at the latest), and the blip ends
            const float target = fabsf(wOut * ratioOf(to));
            if (gear != to)
            {
                gear = 0;
                if ((t >= 0.015f && w >= 0.98f * target) || t >= 0.1f)
                {
                    gear = to;
                    tIn = t;
                }
            }
            blip = gear == to ? 0.0f : target;
            if (gear == to)
                shifting = false;
        }
    }
};

module Bike
{
    VehSpec spec;
    BikeSpec bs;
    VehEnv env;
    VehTel tel;
    BikeTel btel;
    BikeBox box;
    BikeChain drive;
    VehTyreCurve curve;
    VehTyre front;
    VehTyre rear;
    VehStrip strip;
    VehSound snd;

    float rate;
    // the engine
    float jE;
    float iEcfg;        // 1 / jE (step takes the engine's inertia of the moment instead when it is given)
    float peakTq;
    float idleW;
    float redW;
    // what the Spec and the engine made
    float mass;         // bike and rider
    float hCg;          // their centre of mass: height, and ahead of the rear contact
    float bCg;
    float wb;
    float radius;
    float jw;
    float iw;
    float jO;
    float iO;
    float clutchCap;
    float eff;
    float sinG;
    float cosG;
    float dragK;
    float mu;
    float brakeMaxF;
    float brakeMaxR;
    float gearSeen;
    bool dirty;
    // the controls
    float engage;
    float brakeIn;
    float pedalIn;      // the rear brake pedal
    float pedal;
    int mode;
    int lastStrip;
    bool stripSeen;
    float kPedal;
    // the couplings the step uses
    float gA;
    float capA;         // forward
    float capBack;      // backward (the slipper's)
    float capDrag;      // what the open clutch's oil passes
    float holdF;
    float holdR;
    float absF;
    float absR;
    // the state
    double wo;
    double wf;          // the front wheel
    double wr;          // the rear wheel
    double v;
    double x;
    double vPrev;
    float aNow;
    float aLag;
    float theta;        // the pitch, rad, nose up
    float thetaRate;
    bool looped;
    bool stoppie;
    float fzF;
    float fzR;
    float aWheelie;
    float throttleK;    // the wheelie control's share of the throttle
    float capWheelie;   // the clutch's capacity it allows (N m at the crank; large: none)
    bool holding;
    float tsh;          // the chain's torque, last sample
    float tClutch;
    float slipC;
    float backMax;      // the most back torque since the telemetry was last written
    float slipMax;
    bool slipping;
    float wLast;
    float lashNow;      // the chain's strike this sample

    void setup(float hostRate)
    {
        rate = hostRate;
        snd.setup(rate);
        jE = 0.05f;
        iEcfg = 1.0f / jE;
        peakTq = 100.0f;
        idleW = 120.0f;
        redW = 1300.0f;
        lastStrip = 0;
        stripSeen = false;
        apply();
        reset();
    }

    void reset()
    {
        box.reset();
        strip.reset();
        drive.reset();
        wo = 0.0;
        wf = 0.0;
        wr = 0.0;
        v = 0.0;
        x = 0.0;
        vPrev = 0.0;
        aNow = 0.0f;
        aLag = 0.0f;
        theta = 0.0f;
        thetaRate = 0.0f;
        looped = false;
        stoppie = false;
        throttleK = 1.0f;
        capWheelie = 1.0e9f;
        holding = false;
        tsh = 0.0f;
        tClutch = 0.0f;
        slipC = 0.0f;
        backMax = 0.0f;
        slipMax = 0.0f;
        slipping = false;
        engage = 1.0f;
        brakeIn = 0.0f;
        pedalIn = 0.0f;
        pedal = 0.0f;
        gA = 0.0f;
        capA = 0.0f;
        capBack = 0.0f;
        capDrag = 0.0f;
        holdF = 0.0f;
        holdR = 0.0f;
        absF = 1.0f;
        absR = 1.0f;
        gearSeen = -1.0f;
        lashNow = 0.0f;
        front.reset(env.temperature);
        rear.reset(env.temperature);
        loads(0.0f);
    }

    void configure(float jEngine, float peak, float idle, float red)
    {
        jE = fmaxf(jEngine, 0.005f);
        iEcfg = 1.0f / jE;
        peakTq = fmaxf(peak, 5.0f);
        idleW = idle;
        redW = fmaxf(red, idle + 50.0f);
        clutchCap = spec.clutchTorque > 0.0f ? spec.clutchTorque : 1.35f * peakTq;
    }

    void apply()
    {
        const float mb = fmaxf(spec.mass, 50.0f);
        const float mr = fmaxf(bs.riderMass, 0.0f);
        mass = mb + mr;
        wb = fmaxf(spec.wheelbase, 0.5f);
        const float tk = fminf(fmaxf(bs.tuck, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        const float hr = bs.riderHeight - 0.12f * tk;
        const float br = (bs.riderForward + 0.06f * tk) * wb;
        hCg = (mb * spec.cgHeight + mr * hr) / mass;
        bCg = (mb * spec.frontWeight * wb + mr * br) / mass;
        radius = fmaxf(spec.tyreRadius, 0.1f);
        jw = fmaxf(spec.wheelInertia, 0.05f);
        iw = 1.0f / jw;
        const float g = env.grade;
        cosG = 1.0f / sqrtf(1.0f + g * g);
        sinG = g * cosG;
        dragK = 0.5f * env.density * (spec.cdA + (bs.cdATuck - spec.cdA) * tk);
        const int tyreKind = bs.bikeTyre < 0 ? 0 : (bs.bikeTyre >= BIKE_TYRES ? BIKE_TYRES - 1 : bs.bikeTyre);
        const int compound = BIKE_TYRE_COMPOUND[tyreKind];
        curve.make(compound);
        mu = BIKE_TYRE_MU[tyreKind] * vehSurfaceGrip(compound, env.surface);
        eff = spec.gearEfficiency * bs.chainEfficiency;
        brakeMaxF = spec.brakeDecel * 9.81f * mass * radius;
        brakeMaxR = (1.0f - spec.brakeBias) * spec.brakeDecel * 9.81f * mass * radius;
        clutchCap = spec.clutchTorque > 0.0f ? spec.clutchTorque : 1.35f * peakTq;
        // the chain's spring: the vehicle model's rule for a car's shafts, by the mass
        drive.k = 9.0f * mass;
        drive.lash = 0.5f * fmaxf(bs.chainLash, 0.0f);
        // the gearbox
        const int n = spec.gears < 1 ? 1 : (spec.gears > VEH_GEARS ? VEH_GEARS : spec.gears);
        if (n != box.n)
            box.reset();
        box.n = n;
        for (int i = 0; i < VEH_GEARS; ++i)
        {
            if (spec.autoGearing)
            {
                if (n == 6)
                    box.r[i] = i < 6 ? BIKE_RATIOS[i] : 1.0f;
                else
                {
                    const float f = n > 1 ? (float)(i < n ? i : n - 1) / (float)(n - 1) : 0.0f;
                    box.r[i] = 2.62f * expf(f * logf(1.18f / 2.62f));
                }
            }
            else
                box.r[i] = spec.ratio[i] > 0.0f ? spec.ratio[i] : 1.0f;
        }
        box.primary = fmaxf(bs.primaryRatio, 0.5f);
        box.chain = (float)(bs.rearSprocket > 1 ? bs.rearSprocket : 1) / (float)(bs.frontSprocket > 1 ? bs.frontSprocket : 1);
        box.cutTime = bs.quickshiftCut;
        dirty = true;
    }

    // The output's inertia and the chain's damping for the gear in
    void driveline()
    {
        const float g = box.shifting ? box.ratioOf(box.to) : box.ratioOf(box.gear);
        if (g == gearSeen && !dirty)
            return;
        dirty = false;
        gearSeen = g;
        // the rear sprocket, the chain and the cush drive's carrier at the wheel (judgement: 0.05 kg m^2); the clutch's
        // basket and plates, the gearbox's shafts and the front sprocket at the crank's side (judgement: 0.004 kg m^2)
        jO = 0.05f + 0.004f * g * g;
        iO = 1.0f / jO;
        const float j1 = jE * g * g + jO;
        const float j2 = mass * radius * radius + 2.0f * jw;
        drive.c = g != 0.0f ? 0.8f * sqrtf(drive.k * j1 * j2 / (j1 + j2)) : 0.0f;
    }

    // ---- every 16 samples ----

    void loads(float d16)
    {
        const float w = mass * 9.81f * cosG;
        // the centre of mass relative to the rear contact, at the pitch now
        const float cs = cosf(theta);
        const float sn = sinf(theta);
        const float xr = bCg * cs - hCg * sn;
        const float yr = bCg * sn + hCg * cs;
        const float a = aNow + 9.81f * sinG;
        // the moment that lifts the front about the rear contact (the weight's against the push's)
        const float lift = mass * a * yr - w * xr;
        aWheelie = hCg > 0.0f ? 9.81f * cosG * bCg / hCg - 9.81f * sinG : 1.0e9f;
        if (theta > 0.0f || lift > 0.0f)
        {
            const float ip = bs.pitchInertia + mass * (xr * xr + yr * yr);
            thetaRate += lift / ip * d16;
            theta += thetaRate * d16;
            if (theta <= 0.0f)
            {
                theta = 0.0f;
                thetaRate = 0.0f;
            }
            const float top = 1.3962634f;   // 80 degrees: the tail on the road
            if (theta > top)
            {
                theta = top;
                thetaRate = 0.0f;
            }
            if (xr <= 0.0f)
                looped = true;
        }
        if (theta > 0.0f)
        {
            fzF = 0.0f;
            fzR = w;
            stoppie = false;
        }
        else
        {
            // both wheels down: the load moves with the acceleration, lagged by the suspension
            fzF = (w * bCg - mass * (aLag + 9.81f * sinG) * hCg) / wb;
            fzF = fmaxf(fzF, 0.0f);
            fzR = w - fzF;
            stoppie = fzR < 0.0f;
            if (stoppie)
            {
                fzR = 0.0f;
                fzF = w;
            }
        }
        front.control(fzF, mu, &curve, curve.compound, v, env.temperature, d16);
        rear.control(fzR, mu, &curve, curve.compound, v, env.temperature, d16);
    }

    // The wheelie control: the throttle's share, or the clutch's capacity, that holds the front at its angle
    void wheelieControl(float d16)
    {
        const float target = bs.wheelieAngle * 0.017453293f;
        holding = false;
        throttleK = fminf(throttleK + d16 / 0.4f, 1.0f);
        capWheelie = 1.0e9f;
        if (bs.wheelieControl == 1)
        {
            // easing the throttle: on the angle beyond the target and the rate it lifts at (a rider's or an
            // anti-wheelie control's loop: judgement, holds a superbike in first within a few degrees)
            const float u = theta - target + 0.25f * thetaRate;
            if (theta > 0.0f && u > 0.0f)
            {
                throttleK = fminf(throttleK, fmaxf(1.0f - 6.0f * u, 0.0f));
                holding = true;
            }
            // and the rear spinning past its peak (a rider rolls off; so does a traction control)
            const float spin = rear.kappa - 1.3f * curve.kPeak;
            if (spin > 0.0f)
                throttleK = fminf(throttleK, fmaxf(1.0f - 4.0f * spin, 0.2f));
        }
        else if (bs.wheelieControl == 2 && gA > 0.0f)
        {
            // slipping the clutch: the push whose pitch acceleration returns the angle to the target, damped
            const float cs = cosf(theta);
            const float sn = sinf(theta);
            const float xr = bCg * cs - hCg * sn;
            const float yr = fmaxf(bCg * sn + hCg * cs, 0.05f);
            const float ip = bs.pitchInertia + mass * (xr * xr + yr * yr);
            const float want = -25.0f * (theta - target) - 10.0f * thetaRate;
            const float aDes = (ip * want + mass * 9.81f * cosG * xr) / (mass * yr) - 9.81f * sinG;
            const float fLim = fmaxf(mass * aDes + dragK * (float)(v * v), 0.0f);
            // and no more than the rear tyre grips (a rider feathering the clutch keeps it hooked up)
            const float fGrip = 0.97f * rear.d;
            capWheelie = fminf(fLim, fGrip) * radius / (gA * eff);
            holding = capWheelie < clutchCap * engage * box.robot && fLim < fGrip;
        }
    }

    // Every 16 samples: the controls (02-contracts.md section 4; lever ignored)
    void control(float d16, float throttle, float clutch, float brake, float handbrake, int up, int down, int ctlMode,
                 int stripCount)
    {
        kPedal = 1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.02f);
        mode = ctlMode;
        pedal = fminf(fmaxf(throttle, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        // the lever: bites a third of the way out, in at three quarters (the vehicle model's)
        const float upC = 1.0f - fminf(fmaxf(clutch, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        const float xc = fminf(fmaxf((upC - 0.32f) / 0.43f, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        engage += (xc * xc * (3.0f - 2.0f * xc) - engage) * kPedal;
        const float b = fminf(fmaxf(brake, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        brakeIn += (b * sqrtf(b) - brakeIn) * kPedal;
        const float p = fminf(fmaxf(handbrake, 0.0f), 1.0f);
        pedalIn += (p - pedalIn) * kPedal;
        if (!stripSeen)
        {
            stripSeen = true;
            lastStrip = stripCount;
        }
        if (stripCount != lastStrip)
        {
            lastStrip = stripCount;
            if (stripCount > 0)
                stage();
        }
        strip.control(d16, x, spec.proTree);
        box.control(d16, up, down, pedal, wLast, (float)wo, idleW, redW, bs.quickshifter, bs.autoBlip, engage);
        driveline();
        gA = box.ratioOf(box.gear);
        wheelieControl(d16);
        const float c = clutchCap * engage * box.robot;
        capA = fminf(c, capWheelie);
        capBack = bs.slipper ? fminf(capA, bs.slipperTorque * clutchCap) : capA;
        capDrag = bs.clutchDry ? 0.0f : 0.006f * clutchCap;
        // the brakes: the lever on the front, the pedal on the rear; ABS lets a wheel off past its tyre's peak
        bool absOn = false;
        const float wantF = brakeMaxF * brakeIn;
        const float wantR = brakeMaxR * pedalIn;
        if (spec.abs && fabsf((float)v) > 1.5f)
        {
            if (wantF > 0.0f && front.kappa < -1.2f * curve.kPeak)
            {
                absF *= 0.6f;
                absOn = true;
            }
            else
                absF = fminf(absF + 0.15f, 1.0f);
            if (wantR > 0.0f && rear.kappa < -1.2f * curve.kPeak)
            {
                absR *= 0.6f;
                absOn = true;
            }
            else
                absR = fminf(absR + 0.15f, 1.0f);
        }
        else
        {
            absF = 1.0f;
            absR = 1.0f;
        }
        holdF = wantF * absF + front.roll * radius;
        holdR = wantR * absR + rear.roll * radius;
        const bool locked = fabsf((float)v) > 1.0f
                            && (fabsf((float)wf) * radius < 0.05f * fabsf((float)v) || fabsf((float)wr) * radius < 0.05f * fabsf((float)v));
        aNow = (float)(v - vPrev) / d16;
        vPrev = v;
        aLag += (aNow - aLag) * (1.0f - expf(-d16 / 0.03f));
        loads(d16);
        telemetry(absOn, locked);
    }

    void stage()
    {
        v = 0.0;
        vPrev = 0.0;
        x = 0.0;
        aLag = 0.0f;
        wf = 0.0;
        wr = 0.0;
        wo = 0.0;
        front.u = 0.0;
        front.rate = 0.0f;
        rear.u = 0.0;
        rear.rate = 0.0f;
        drive.reset();
        theta = 0.0f;
        thetaRate = 0.0f;
        strip.stage(spec.proTree);
    }

    void telemetry(bool absOn, bool locked)
    {
        tel.speed = (float)v;
        tel.accel = aNow;
        tel.distance = (float)x;
        tel.gear = box.gear;
        tel.shift = box.shifting ? (box.up ? 1 : 2) : 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < VEH_WHEELS; ++i)
        {
            tel.wheelSpeed[i] = 0.0f;
            tel.wheelSlip[i] = 0.0f;
            tel.wheelLoad[i] = 0.0f;
            tel.wheelForce[i] = 0.0f;
            tel.wheelTorque[i] = 0.0f;
            tel.wheelTemp[i] = 0.0f;
        }
        tel.wheelSpeed[0] = (float)wf;
        tel.wheelSlip[0] = front.kappa;
        tel.wheelLoad[0] = front.fz;
        tel.wheelForce[0] = front.force;
        tel.wheelTemp[0] = front.temp;
        tel.wheelSpeed[2] = (float)wr;
        tel.wheelSlip[2] = rear.kappa;
        tel.wheelLoad[2] = rear.fz;
        tel.wheelForce[2] = rear.force;
        tel.wheelTorque[2] = tsh;
        tel.wheelTemp[2] = rear.temp;
        int flags = 0;
        if (rear.kappa > 1.5f * curve.kPeak)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_SPIN;
        if (theta > 0.0f)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_WHEELIE;
        if (absOn)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_ABS;
        if (locked)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_LOCKED;
        if (box.shifting)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_SHIFT;
        if (box.cut)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_CUT;
        if (box.blip > 0.0f)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_BLIP;
        if (rear.d > 0.0f && fabsf(rear.force) >= 0.9f * rear.d)
            flags |= VEH_FLAG_LIMIT;
        tel.flags = flags;
        tel.clutchSlip = slipC;
        tel.shaftTorque = tsh;
        tel.wheelPower = tsh * (float)wr;
        tel.pitch = mass * aLag * hCg / wb;
        tel.ratio = gA;
        tel.stripState = strip.state;
        tel.tReaction = strip.reaction;
        tel.t60 = strip.et[0];
        tel.t330 = strip.et[1];
        tel.t660 = strip.et[3];
        tel.v660 = strip.v660;
        tel.t1000 = strip.et[4];
        tel.t1320 = strip.et[6];
        tel.v1320 = strip.v1320;
        int bf = 0;
        if (rear.kappa < -1.2f * curve.kPeak && v > 2.0)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_HOP;
        if (looped)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_LOOPED;
        if (holding)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_HOLDING;
        if (slipping)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_SLIPPER;
        if (box.cut)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_QUICKSHIFT;
        if (box.blip > 0.0f)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_BLIP;
        if (stoppie)
            bf |= BIKE_FLAG_STOPPIE;
        btel.bikeFlags = bf;
        btel.liftAngle = theta * 57.29578f;
        btel.liftRate = thetaRate * 57.29578f;
        btel.chainLash = drive.events;
        btel.chainLashSpeed = drive.speed;
        btel.chainLashSide = drive.side;
        btel.backTorque = backMax;
        btel.slipperSlip = slipMax;
        btel.quickshifts = box.quickshifts;
        btel.blips = box.blips;
        btel.wheelieLimit = aWheelie;
        btel.sprocketSpeed = (float)wo * box.chain;
        backMax = 0.0f;
        slipMax = 0.0f;
        slipping = false;
    }

    // ---- one sample ----

    // jCrank: the crank's inertia this sample (a custom engine's moving masses vary it round the turn, and their inertia
    // torque is in tq: stepped with any other inertia that torque makes energy, finding X-007), 0 for configure's
    float step(float w, float tq, float dt, float jCrank)
    {
        const float idt = 1.0f / dt;
        const float iE = jCrank > 0.0f ? 1.0f / jCrank : iEcfg;
        const float vf = (float)v;
        // the tyres, from their deflections as they stand
        const float ff = front.push(&curve, (float)wf * radius, vf);
        const float fr = rear.push(&curve, (float)wr * radius, vf);
        float tf = -ff * radius;
        float tr = -fr * radius;
        // the chain
        const bool inGear = gA != 0.0f;
        float ts = 0.0f;
        if (inGear)
            ts = drive.torque((float)(wo - wr));
        else
            drive.strike = 0.0f;
        lashNow = drive.strike;
        if (lashNow > 0.0f)
            snd.strike(lashNow);
        tsh = ts;
        tr += ts;
        // the clutch: the torque that holds the crank to the output through the ratio, within its capacity forward
        // and the slipper's backward; open, its oil's drag
        float te = tq;
        float to = -ts;
        float tc = 0.0f;
        float fA = 0.0f;
        if (inGear)
        {
            const float num = (float)(w - gA * wo) * idt + te * iE - gA * to * iO;
            const float f = num * w >= 0.0f ? gA * eff : gA / eff;
            const float t = num / (iE + gA * f * iO);
            const float hi = fmaxf(capA, capDrag);
            const float lo = fmaxf(capBack, capDrag);
            tc = fminf(fmaxf(t, -lo), hi);
            if (t < -lo && lo > 0.0f && bs.slipper && capBack < capA)
                slipping = true;
            fA = tc * w >= 0.0f ? gA * eff : gA / eff;
            te -= tc;
            to += fA * tc;
            backMax = fmaxf(backMax, -tc);
        }
        tClutch = tc;
        slipC = w - gA * (float)wo;
        if (inGear)
            slipMax = fmaxf(slipMax, slipping ? fabsf(slipC) : 0.0f);
        // the brakes and the rolling hold each wheel
        const float thF = fminf(fmaxf((float)wf * jw * idt + tf, -holdF), holdF);
        const float thR = fminf(fmaxf((float)wr * jw * idt + tr, -holdR), holdR);
        tf -= thF;
        tr -= thR;
        // every speed moves
        float wn = w + te * iE * dt;
        if (wn < 0.0f)
            wn = 0.0f;
        double won = wo + (double)(to * iO * dt);
        wf += (double)(tf * iw * dt);
        wr += (double)(tr * iw * dt);
        const float fAir = dragK * vf * fabsf(vf);
        const float fHill = mass * 9.81f * sinG;
        v += (double)((ff + fr - fAir - fHill) / mass * dt);
        if (!inGear)
        {
            won = wr;
            drive.twist = 0.0f;
        }
        else
            drive.advance((float)(won - wr), dt);
        front.advance((float)wf * radius, (float)v, dt);
        rear.advance((float)wr * radius, (float)v, dt);
        x += v * (double)dt;
        wo = won;
        wLast = wn;
        return wn;
    }

    float road()
    {
        const float uf = fabsf(front.slipV);
        const float ur = fabsf(rear.slipV);
        const float sq = fminf(fmaxf((uf - 1.2f) / 4.0f, 0.0f), 1.0f) * 0.3f + fminf(fmaxf((ur - 1.2f) / 4.0f, 0.0f), 1.0f) * 0.7f;
        // (two tyres: half the rumble of a car's four)
        return snd.tick((float)v, env.surface, sq);
    }

    // ---- for the engine ----

    // The throttle the engine is given: the rider's, less what the wheelie control and a clutch upshift take, with an
    // auto-blip's (wAvg: the crank's mean speed, rad/s)
    float pedalOut(float gas, float wAvg)
    {
        float p = gas * throttleK * box.rollOff;
        if (box.blip > 0.0f)
            p = fmaxf(p, fminf(fmaxf((box.blip - wAvg) * 0.05f, 0.0f), 1.0f));
        return p;
    }

    bool cutWanted()
    {
        return box.cut;
    }

    float blipSpeed()
    {
        return box.blip;
    }

    float slip()
    {
        return rear.kappa;
    }

    float lashStrike()
    {
        return lashNow;
    }

    // the front sprocket's speed (the gearbox's output), rad/s
    float sprocketSpeed()
    {
        return (float)wo * box.chain;
    }

    // the gearbox's own ratio in the gear in (0 in neutral and while the dogs are out)
    float gearboxRatio()
    {
        if (box.gear <= 0)
            return 0.0f;
        return box.r[(box.gear > box.n ? box.n : box.gear) - 1];
    }

    // the gearbox's input shaft (the clutch's hub), rad/s: the output through the gear; in neutral the clutch's basket
    // (the crank over the primary drive), as an engaged clutch turns it
    float gearboxInput()
    {
        const float g = gearboxRatio();
        return g > 0.0f ? sprocketSpeed() * g : wLast / box.primary;
    }
};
